From cb4733773e4938ea315fc7590653c1ac483fd4a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard DEMONGEOT <richard@rdem-systems.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:34:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 62/74] gui: report backend and status messages in the selected
 language (issue #10)

Many messages produced by the Go side (progress, errors, job history)
and a dozen status messages in App.jsx were hard-coded in French, so an
English UI showed e.g. "Session PBS perdue, attente ... avant retry".

- Go: user-facing messages are now English, like the rest of the
  backend output; tests updated to match.
- api/cancel.go: still recognise the old French cancellation text.
- App.jsx: hard-coded status messages go through t(), with new keys in
  the five UI languages.
